  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 145 PM MST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThursday...Expect a decent warming trend as a well pronounced ridge \naloft builds across the western High Plains states from the western \nDakotas southward to eastern Colorado. 700 mb temperatures near 2 \nCelsius will yield maximum temperatures in the 50s.\n\nFriday...A progressive shortwave trough aloft will move across \neastern Montana and the western Dakotas, but only with some mid and \nhigh level clouds across our counties and limited lift producing no \nprecipitation.\n\nSaturday...The trough aloft moves into Nebraska and Kansas with a \nshortwave ridge aloft moving over Wyoming, continuing the dry \nweather for our forecast area.\n\nSunday...The flow aloft backs to westerly, inducing a decent surface \nlee trough across eastern Wyoming and eastern Colorado and producing \na warming trend. 700 mb temperatures near 6 Celsius will yield high \ntemperatures from the mid 50s to upper 60s.\n\nMonday-Tuesday...Dry westerly flow aloft will continue with a \nprogressive pattern of fast moving shortwave troughs aloft moving \nacross our forecast area, but producing no precipitation due to \nrelatively dry low and mid levels. Maximum temperatures will \ncontinue above normal, from the upper 50s to mid 60s.",
